# Spec Writing (spec folders + multi-perspective spec model)

Every change with something to decide gets a **spec folder**: `specs/NNN-<slug>/` with `spec.md`
(WHAT and WHY), `plan.md` (HOW), and `tasks.md` (commit-sized tasks). Templates in
`specs/_templates/`; the process in `specs/README.md`; the spec model in `docs/SPEC-MODEL.md`.

## spec.md — six parts

| Part | Sections |
|---|---|
| **1. Intent** | Business [REQUIRED], Functional [REQUIRED] (user stories, numbered ACs, edge cases), Out of scope [REQUIRED] |
| **2. User experience** | Design (if UI), Accessibility [REQUIRED if UI] |
| **3. Non-functional** | Security [REQUIRED], Privacy [REQUIRED if personal data], Performance, SEO, Analytics, Localization |
| **4. Constraints** | Constraints & prior decisions (business rules, compliance, ADRs/PDRs to respect) |
| **5. Validation & delivery** | Testing [REQUIRED], Documentation [REQUIRED] (pre- and post-implementable), Observability, Deployment |
| **6. Meta** | Clarifications [REQUIRED], References |

A section is filled with concrete content, "Standard project [area] applies", or "Not applicable:
[reason]". Optional sections that don't apply are left out.

## plan.md and tasks.md

- `plan.md`: constitution check, approach, architecture & integrations, **change surface** (every file
  and layer, verified by reading the code), data & contracts, test strategy (every AC → a test),
  documentation plan, rollout, risks, **assumptions**, open questions.
- `tasks.md`: one task per commit, in dependency order; each names its test and the ACs it serves;
  docs-first tasks before implementation tasks; a Gate results section for evidence.

## Rules

- Requirements come from the tracker task or the requester — if neither states them, stop and ask. Never invent them.
- Link the tracker task in frontmatter; never copy its text.
- WHAT and WHY in `spec.md`; HOW in `plan.md`. No code or file paths in Business or Functional.
- Every AC is numbered and independently testable; numbers never change.
- Change requests on delivered work **amend the same folder** with a `CR N` section (intent + Delivered → Change table) and new ACs tagged `(CR N)`. If the delta can't be recovered, ask.
- **Approval gate:** after plan and tasks, stop and show the developer the scope, the change surface, and the assumptions. Only the developer approves (`status: approved` + an `approvals:` line). Then commit the folder with `spec:`.
- Workflow after approval: docs first (`docs:`) → one task per commit (test red → green) → reconcile docs → gate results → draft PR when asked.
